  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656094",
      "title": "Getting Access to the Template & DOM with @ViewChild",
      "lectureOrder": 399,
      "videoOrder": 368,
      "sourceHash": "9e455190e764da0f6e14474221213a79bf83fb013586c9874227a13afcde7d99",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.4,
          "end": 5.783,
          "en": "-: In the last lecture, we learned about local references.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.783,
          "end": 9.347,
          "en": "Now ,there is also another way of getting access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.347,
          "end": 14.347,
          "en": "to local references or to any element, actually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 14.37,
          "end": 17.19,
          "en": "directly from within our TypeScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.19,
          "end": 19.83,
          "en": "Right now, we're passing the reference here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.83,
          "end": 24.18,
          "en": "when we call a method, and that works fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.18,
          "end": 25.92,
          "en": "but sometimes you want to get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.92,
          "end": 27.81,
          "en": "before we call a method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.81,
          "end": 30.15,
          "en": "And there is a nice little decorator we can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.15,
          "end": 32.61,
          "en": "in TypeScript to get this access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.61,
          "end": 35.7,
          "en": "Let's do the same 4D server content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.7,
          "end": 39.06,
          "en": "So here, I will quickly duplicate that input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.06,
          "end": 42.57,
          "en": "and comment out the old solution using two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.57,
          "end": 45.935,
          "en": "and the new solution will not use two-way binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.935,
          "end": 49.8,
          "en": "but instead this will now also have a local reference,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.8,
          "end": 52.383,
          "en": "this server content input, maybe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.28,
          "end": 56.28,
          "en": "Now, in the cockpit component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.28,
          "end": 59.319,
          "en": "I will also comment out the old new server content here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.319,
          "end": 62.07,
          "en": "and I will add a new property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.07,
          "end": 66.963,
          "en": "which I'll name server content input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.03999999999999,
          "end": 70.895,
          "en": "Now, server content input like this is just a property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.895,
          "end": 74.85,
          "en": "but we can add at View Child in front of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.85,
          "end": 76.77,
          "en": "this decorator with parenthesis",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.77,
          "end": 81.77,
          "en": "and we need to import View Child from at Angular Core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.26,
          "end": 84.45,
          "en": "Now, View Child like this won't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.45,
          "end": 86.37,
          "en": "We need to pass an argument here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.37,
          "end": 90.72,
          "en": "And this argument actually is the selector of the element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.72,
          "end": 92.577,
          "en": "How we want to select the element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.577,
          "end": 96.45,
          "en": "And selector now, not like a CSS selector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.45,
          "end": 98.72999999999999,
          "en": "but for example, we can simply pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.72999999999999,
          "end": 102.27000000000001,
          "en": "as a string, the name of a local reference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.27000000000001,
          "end": 107.27000000000001,
          "en": "So, server content input could now be passed as a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.28,
          "end": 108.96000000000001,
          "en": "If you don't want to pass a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.96000000000001,
          "end": 110.654,
          "en": "but want to select a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.654,
          "end": 114.45,
          "en": "you could simply pass the component type here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.45,
          "end": 117,
          "en": "So, in the cockpit we don't use any other components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117,
          "end": 120.42,
          "en": "but in the app component we could pass cockpit component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.42,
          "end": 122.79,
          "en": "so the type like this, not like a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.79,
          "end": 125.7,
          "en": "to get access to the first occurrence",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.7,
          "end": 128.97,
          "en": "of this cockpit component in the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.97,
          "end": 130.35,
          "en": "But here, I'll switch this back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.35,
          "end": 132.57,
          "en": "to getting access to the local reference,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.57,
          "end": 137.25,
          "en": "which probably is the use case you'll see the most often.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.25,
          "end": 140.16,
          "en": "And with that, we now get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.16,
          "end": 143.46,
          "en": "to our server content input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.46,
          "end": 145.749,
          "en": "Now what does this actually hold then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.749,
          "end": 147.99,
          "en": "Let's quickly comment out this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.99,
          "end": 150.03,
          "en": "so that it doesn't break.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.03,
          "end": 154.38,
          "en": "And let's log this server content input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.38,
          "end": 155.49,
          "en": "So, our property here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.49,
          "end": 159.69,
          "en": "which is kind of set through View Child.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.69,
          "end": 163.17000000000002,
          "en": "So with this, if I also comment this out down here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.17000000000002,
          "end": 164.61,
          "en": "so that we can run our app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.61,
          "end": 167.49,
          "en": "And if I now save this and we go back to our application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.49,
          "end": 169.98,
          "en": "and I enter something here and I click ad server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.98,
          "end": 173.91,
          "en": "we see that this is of type, element ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.91,
          "end": 175.53,
          "en": "So unlike the local reference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.53,
          "end": 178.98,
          "en": "we passed directly from the template via the method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.98,
          "end": 181.41,
          "en": "which was the element itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.41,
          "end": 184.05,
          "en": "this is of type, element ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 184.05,
          "end": 186.06,
          "en": "So, we can set this type here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 186.06,
          "end": 189.51,
          "en": "Element ref, a reference to that element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.51,
          "end": 192.78,
          "en": "Element ref needs to be imported from at Angular Core,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.78,
          "end": 195.017,
          "en": "it's a Angular type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 195.017,
          "end": 197.37,
          "en": "So, this element ref, however,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.37,
          "end": 200.76,
          "en": "has a useful property we can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 200.76,
          "end": 203.76,
          "en": "and that's the native element property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.76,
          "end": 206.73,
          "en": "We can use server content, whoops",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 206.73,
          "end": 209.25,
          "en": "this server content input here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 209.25,
          "end": 211.2,
          "en": "and then native element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 211.2,
          "end": 213.465,
          "en": "to get access to the underlying element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 213.465,
          "end": 215.1,
          "en": "which now has a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 215.1,
          "end": 217.893,
          "en": "because this will now be the input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 218.79,
          "end": 220.47,
          "en": "Now we can do the same, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 220.47,
          "end": 223.47,
          "en": "for the on-app blueprint method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 223.47,
          "end": 227.67000000000002,
          "en": "and with this, we get direct access to elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 227.67000000000002,
          "end": 232.05,
          "en": "in our DOM, in our template through at View Child.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 232.05,
          "end": 234.72899999999998,
          "en": "And you should see that this now works again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 234.72899999999998,
          "end": 238.65,
          "en": "if we enter some content here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 238.65,
          "end": 241.11,
          "en": "and click the buttons, works perfectly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 241.11,
          "end": 242.79,
          "en": "Now without two-way binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 242.79,
          "end": 244.8,
          "en": "but with local references passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 244.8,
          "end": 249.8,
          "en": "to methods or local references fetched through View Child.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 250.408,
          "end": 252.6,
          "en": "Now, one important thing to watch out for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 252.6,
          "end": 256.71,
          "en": "is you should not change the element through this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 256.71,
          "end": 261.15,
          "en": "Because of chorus, you could use our server content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 261.15,
          "end": 262.59,
          "en": "input the native element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 262.59,
          "end": 264.924,
          "en": "and then set value to something, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 264.924,
          "end": 266.4,
          "en": "You can do this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 266.4,
          "end": 269.01,
          "en": "And if we actually do this like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 269.01,
          "end": 270.9,
          "en": "and I click add server blueprint,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 270.9,
          "end": 273.201,
          "en": "you see something was now added here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 273.201,
          "end": 276.69,
          "en": "I strongly recommend not doing this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 276.69,
          "end": 279.65999999999997,
          "en": "You should not access the DOM like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 279.65999999999997,
          "end": 282.99,
          "en": "Angular offers you a better way of accessing the DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 282.99,
          "end": 286.14,
          "en": "and you will learn about this in the directives section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 286.14,
          "end": 287.979,
          "en": "Generally, you should use the other tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 287.979,
          "end": 290.52,
          "en": "like string interpolation and property binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 290.52,
          "end": 292.83,
          "en": "if you want to output something in the DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 292.83,
          "end": 296.67,
          "en": "and not directly mess with any elements you can get,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 296.67,
          "end": 299.913,
          "en": "even though if you have gotten them through Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
